-- `mid` re-exports two unrelated `mth`s, `IG.mth` and `IP.mth`, both `f a -> Int`,
-- and this module imports both through it.  No standalone is in scope, so
-- SHADOW-SEMANTICS.md S2-DECL (d) decides the occurrence over the admitted set (ruled
-- 2026-10-14): each declaration is asked through its own receiver, `W`; `impl IG W`
-- answers and `IP` has no impl, so exactly one selects and the occurrence commits to
-- `IG W`, whose body is 5.  Spec answer: 5 on every verb, the built binary included.
import mid.{IP, IG, mth}

data W a = MkW a

impl IG W where
  mth w = 5

main = println (mth (MkW 1))
